    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "green",
    "description": "Ethan and coaching client, Kristin Cruz, discuss the core questions you must answer before leaving your corporate job:\n\n1. How Reversible Is This Decision?\n2. What Are Your Actual Constraints?\n3. Why Would Anyone Hire You?\n4. What Problem Are You Promising to Solve?\n5. Are You a Vitamin or a Painkiller?\n6. Have You Done This Work on Yourself?\n7. Where Will Your Customers Come From?\n8. What's Your Math?\n9. Can You Handle the Lumpiness?\n10. Who Is Going to Do the Work You Hate?\n11. Where Is the Energy Going to Come From?\n\n---------\nAbout Kristin:\nKristin Cruz is a strategic advisor who helps leaders and teams navigate complexity with greater clarity, stronger alignment, and thoughtful action. Over more than a decade in product and people leadership, she's led successful cross-functional programs, guided teams through significant change, and built a reputation for facilitating honest conversations that help leaders and teams move forward together.\n\nAfter years of leading inside organizations, Kristin is now building an advisory practice centered on helping leaders navigate meaningful transitions with clarity and purpose—whether through strategic partnership, leadership development, or collaborative work alongside executive coaches. In this conversation with Ethan, she'll explore how to build a business around work that's often difficult to measure, but deeply valuable to the leaders and teams who experience it.\n\nConnect with Kristin on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/krcruz/\n\nCollaborate with Kristin: https://www.kristincruzconsulting.com/\n\n---------\nAbout Ethan Evans:\nIn Ethan's 15+ years at Amazon, he led global teams of 800+ and invented well-known businesses and products such as Prime Video, Amazon Video, Amazon Appstore, Merch by Amazon, Prime Gaming (formerly Twitch Prime), and Twitch Commerce. \n\n-- 70+ patents. \n-- Reviewed 10,000+ resumes, conducted 2,500+ interviews, and 1,000+ hires. \n-- Was an Amazon Bar Raiser and Bar Raiser Core Leader, responsible for training and maintaining Amazon's group of interview outcome facilitators. \n-- Helped advocate for and draft the Amazon Leadership Principle (LP) “Ownership” — the words, “They never say ‘that’s not my job.’” are Ethan's. \n\nEthan's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/ \n\nLevel Up Newsletter: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/\n\nLeadership development courses https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
