    "topicLabel": "AI-Era Work & Product Leadership",
    "tags": [
      "AI & automation"
    ],
    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Wt4X8tsXFA",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "orange",
    "description": "What you'll learn:\n1/ Balance AI hype vs real business needs now. As an executive, how do you balance and evaluate AI hype with what your business realistically needs now?\n\n2/ Your sound AI adoption plan for teams. As an executive, how do you manage ongoing disruption and uncertainly around AI?\n\n3/ How to lead by example with GenAI. How does your own use of GenAI act an important model for your org/team as well as a good tool to use in a job search?\n\nWhy this topic matters: GenAI is reshaping how teams build, decide, and compete...fast. Executives who model practical use set the bar for learning and speed, while a clear adoption plan reduces risk and confusion amid constant disruption. Balancing hype with real business needs keeps investment focused, outcomes measurable, and talent (and your job search) sharper.\n\nRead our Level Up article on 'Be AI+: Human Skills for the Machine Age' - https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/p/be-ai-human-skills-for-the-machine\n\nRead Sue's article on 'From Resistance to Resilience: Our Role as Change Agents in AI Adoption' - https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/p/from-resistance-to-resilience-our\n\nAnd if you are interested, join Sue & Ethan's upcoming cohort of Cracking the C-suite in the AI Economy starting on May 2. The course is for current Directors and VPs. Each cohort is limited to 50 seats. And you get invited to ongoing alumni reunions hosted by Sue - https://maven.com/ethan-evans/cracking-the-c-suite\n\n---------\nAbout Ethan Evans\nIn Ethan's 15+ years at Amazon, he led global teams of 800+ and invented well-known businesses and products such as Prime Video, Amazon Video, Amazon Appstore, Merch by Amazon, Prime Gaming (formerly Twitch Prime), and Twitch Commerce. \n\n-- 70+ patents. \n-- Reviewed 10,000+ resumes, conducted 2,500+ interviews, and 1,000+ hires. \n-- Was an Amazon Bar Raiser and Bar Raiser Core Leader, responsible for training and maintaining Amazon's group of interview outcome facilitators. \n-- Helped advocate for and draft the Amazon Leadership Principle (LP) “Ownership” — the words, “They never say ‘that’s not my job.’” are Ethan's. \n\nEthan's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n\nLevel Up Newsletter: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/\n\nLeadership development courses https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)\n\n---------\nAbout Sue Bethanis, Ed.D.\nSusan J. Bethanis, Ed.D., is the CEO/Founder of Mariposa Leadership, Inc., a 15-person San Francisco- based ﬁrm, which provides executive coaching and design thinking to high-tech leaders.\n\nSue is the author of the well-received business book Leadership Chronicles of a Corporate Sage (Kaplan Publishing, 2004) and hosts the popular show WiseTalk, a monthly leadership forum, and WiseSpace, a Zoom coaching community.\n\nSue regularly facilitates strategy offsites and delivers keynotes on inﬂuence, coaching, and innovation. Most recently, Sue has been focused on supporting executives to pivot strategies and enhance culture given the Hybrid/Remote work environment.\n\nUsing real-time, relevant business issues, Sue helps executives:\n\n- Energize their leadership skills that results in increased influence across the organization.\n\n- Energize their leadership teams that results in increased engagement, motivation, and productivity.\n\n- Energize their leadership creativity that results in innovative and sustainable organizational strategies, structures, and culture\n\n​Sue has worked with many Silicon Valley and San Francisco companies and non-profits, including C-level Executives and VPs at Amazon, Apple, Cisco, eBay, EqCA, Expedia, GoFundMe, Google, Guru, HPE, Intel, LinkedIn, Microsoft, MongoDB, Monite, Paypal, Pinterest, Roku, Twitch, Workday, Yahoo!, and Zynga.\n\nSue's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/suebethanis/\n\nMariposa Leadership: https://mariposaleadership.com/",
    "published": "2026-04-03T12:00:56.000Z"
