    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gRb8aeun_7g",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "teal",
    "description": "What you'll learn:\n1/ Pick up difficult problems that needed solutions. Inherit or identify big messes and solve them. Drive 0 to 1 or 1 to N ideas.\n\n2/ Act like an API. Make it your job to translate between teams, orgs, functions, and disconnected problems.\n\n3/ Ask for what you want. Learn to ask \"How can I help you hit your goals\" or \"Would x help you\".\n\n4/ Other key actions: Train your emotions, make your work visible, chose who to work with, ignore hierarchy\n\nContent is designed for early career professionals, ICs and new managers with under 10 years experience, but is applicable to anyone.\n\nIf this content resonated, consider joining Jason & Ethan's new course \"Get Promoted Faster: For Early Career ICs & Managers\" which goes in-depth on The Magic Loop (5-steps for rapid career growth), 7 core \"How To\" skills (with detailed frameworks, action plans, and AI prompts), and 6 steps to leading your promotion conversation: https://maven.com/ethan-evans/early-career-promotion-fast-track\n\n---------\nAbout Jason Yoong\nJason has run multiple $1B+ businesses across eCommerce, marketplaces, advertising, and media. He's led 40+ person organizations, owned department P&L, managed $400M+ marketing budgets, and served as an Advisory Board Member.\n\nAfter leading and building at publicly traded companies Amazon, Dentsu Aegis, and Universal McCann (IPG), Jason joined the founding team of a venture-backed software startup and raised $8M seed.\n\nJason is now building Level Up: Your guide to grow fast, avoid mistakes, and make optimal career moves with Ethan Evans (retired Amazon Vice President). He also serves on the Harvard Business Review advisory council and as a mentor at First Round Capital and Techstars.\n\nSubscribe to the free Level Up Newsletter: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/\n\nJason's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/jasonyoong/\n\n---------\nAbout Shankha Dey\nSr Director, Product @Salesforce Data+AI. Ex- Cortana, Bing, Microsoft Search.\n\nSenior product executive using my AI/ML background to help near or post IPO companies build new products and businesses.\n\nHands-on leadership of top level company objectives with cross-division GMs and C-suite. Investor in various early to mid stage companies.\n\nSkills:\nMaking complex decisions with limited data\nBalancing user impact with business needs\nBeing the calm factor during major incidents\nBuilding consensus across large organizations\n\nI've built and marketed planet-scale products and platforms at Microsoft and Salesforce: agents, enterprise and consumer search, voice assistants, and recommenders. I founded a startup with a visual search product 5 years before Google Lens, and previously worked as an engineer in cybersecurity and finance.\n\nShankha's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/shankhasdey/",
