    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cfcE_1sB60k",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "violet",
    "description": "**Announcement** Maven is offering 20% off our following two courses until June 22nd (Sunday):\n\n- Breakthrough to Executive is for leaders wanting to grow to Principal, Staff, Director, or VP: https://maven.com/ethan-evans/break-through-to-executive?promoCode=MAVEN100\n\n- Get Promoted Faster is for ICs and new managers under 10 years experience who want rapid career growth: https://maven.com/ethan-evans/early-career-promotion-fast-track?promoCode=MAVEN100\n\nIn this 49min Maven Lightning Lesson, you will learn:\n1/ Stripe's standout product management practices — Continuous user engagement, writing-centric culture, and holistic product teams\n\n2/ Amazon's pioneering product management mechanisms — Deep writing culture and \"single threaded leaders.\"\n\n3/ Airbnb's unique product management structure — Laser focus on prioritization, execution, and how it's done.\n\nWhy this topic matters: A great PM ensures the most valuable problem is solved, at the right time, in the right way—maximizing customer impact and business outcomes while aligning teams behind a shared vision. Turn ambiguity into clarity, ideas into strategy, and strategy into results.\n\n---------\nAbout Ethan Evans\n​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​Ethan retired from Amazon as a Vice President after 15 years where he led global teams of 800+ and invented well-known businesses and products such as Prime Video, Amazon Video, Amazon Appstore, Merch by Amazon, Prime Gaming (formerly Twitch Prime), and Twitch Commerce.\n\n​​​​​​​​​​​​-- 70+ patents.\n\n​​​​​​​​​​​​-- Reviewed 10,000+ resumes, conducted 2,500+ interviews, and 1,000+ hires.\n\n​​​​​​​​​​​​-- Was an Amazon Bar Raiser and Bar Raiser Core Leader, responsible for training and maintaining Amazon's group of interview outcome facilitators.\n\n​​​​​​​​​​​​-- Helped advocate for and draft the Amazon Leadership Principle (LP) “Ownership” — the words, “They never say ‘that’s not my job.’” are Ethan's (read the story).\n\n​​​​​Ethan has promoted 8 reports from Senior Manager (Amazon L7) to Director (Amazon L8), contributed to 25+ Director promotions, hired 10+ Directors internally and externally, drove the promotion of 3 engineers to Principal, and of his former reports 2 are current Amazon VPs (L10) and 5 are C-Suite outside of Amazon.\n\n​​​​​Ethan retired from Amazon as a Vice President in September 2020 to focus on paying forward his good fortune to others.\n\n​​​​​Prior to Amazon, Ethan spent 12 years at 3 startups.\n\nEthan's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n\nEthan's free newsletter Level Up: Grow fast, make optimal career moves, avoid mistakes and setbacks, and achieve your financial goals - https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/\n\n---------\nAbout Rohan Kamath (Product@Airbnb | ex - Stripe, Msft, Amzn, Stanford)\nRohan was born somewhere and then he grew up (or so they say). Along the way, he attended a fancy university where he learned about important things like instant-ramen hacks, student loans, and why they call it “foot-ball” instead of “hand-egg”. He then worked for a few famous smartypants who taught him that work could be a lot of fun if he didn’t take himself too seriously. He has been birding since he was 6 years old, but his favorite bird is still a mean Tandoori Chicken.\n\nWhen he’s not writing about himself in the third person, Rohan spends most of his time outdoors hiking and birding in the Pacific Northwest with his wife Pk and his puppy Albus. Rumor has it that he builds products at Airbnb although he not-so-secretly wishes he was a chef so that he could forever feed the foodie kid inside him who refuses to grow up.\n\nHe is extremely passionate about learning new things and obsessively and consistently reads books every day. He also writes on Quora where his work has been read a few times, and on LinkedIn, where people think he's bonkers. He thinks he’s sarcastic and hilarious, however, most people (allegedly) find him obnoxious and annoying.\n\nRohan's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/rohankamath/",
