    "id": "fresh-EtmnXHJl48w",
    "title": "Traits of high performing tech teams with David Markley (Tech VP)",
    "deck": "A new public video from Ethan Evans.",
    "topic": "leadership-management",
    "topicLabel": "Leadership & People Management",
    "tags": [
      "Leadership & management"
    ],
    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EtmnXHJl48w",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "violet",
    "description": "Tech is not the end goal — it's a means to business success. In this lightning lesson by David Markley (Warner Bros; Amazon) you'll learn how to setup your team tech to succeed and drive business outcomes.\n\nKey topics:\n-How to setup a high performing tech team\n-How to turnaround a low performing tech team\n-How to challenge your tech team\n-How to align tech and business initiatives and success\n- Audience questions\n\nIf you want to go deeper on how to deliver big tech projects and lead large cross-functional teams successfully, explore David and Ethan's course: https://maven.com/ethan-evans/excel-as-a-technology-executive\n\nThe next cohort starts June 7th. Enroll by May 4th to get the early bird discount, use code SHIPITEARLYBIRD at checkout. \n\n-----\nAbout David Markley\nIn my 20+ years as a technical executive (after 10+ years as an engineer), I led tech teams as the VP of Technology at Eurosport, Warner Bros, Discovery Inc, MotorTrend Group, Sweetgreen.\n\nPrior, I served as Head of Global Developer Relations at Amazon for 7+ years, was the CTO of Outrigger Media, Chief Architect of AOL, and more.\n\n--100+ tech products launched (20+ new products and 80+ significant product improvements or events)\n--Led 300+ tech teams.\n--Promoted 10+ reports to Director of Eng or VP of Technology and hired 20+ people into those roles.\n--Hold 12+ patents.\n--Have 1:1 coached 100+ tech leaders.\n--Was an Amazon Bar Raiser, reviewed 8,000+ resumes, conducted 2,000+ interviews, and have been part of hiring 1,000+ people across multiple job functions.\n--Helped create and launch the Hiring Champions program for Warner Bros. Discovery (WBD) that greatly improved the quality of the people they hired.\n--Shipped support for the 2024 Olympic Games in Paris for Warner Brother's online sports network—47 markets, 19 languages, 215M viewers, 54 concurrent live streams (the course will include my recent global project implementation lessons).\n\nI am a retired Major from the Army National Guard and led Engineer organizations (both combat and construction). I've commanded units during two natural disaster recovery operations and prepared logistics for a third: severe flooding in Ohio, hurricane relief in Virginia, and planned for post-Katrina. The military provided excellent training and real world experience in leadership, coaching, program management, and operating within a crisis. I carried that experience with me into my civilian career.\n\nI have served six weeks abroad for the Army, but never in a combat zone. Both times it was for construction operations and \"nation building,\" once in Germany and once in Jamaica (post-hurricane Gilbert recovery).\n\nI am passionate about working with technically gifted people to create magical experiences that impact large communities.\n\nOver the years, I have found that growing and developing people gives me a great deal of joy; especially when they go on to surpass my expectations. When they create technology that engages and delights others, I know that I have had a lasting impact.\n\nFind me on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/davidmarkley/\n\n---------\nAbout Level Up\nLevel Up is your source for executive insights, high performance habits, and specific career growth actions with Ethan Evans (retired Amazon VP; LinkedIn Top Voice) and Jason Yoong (COO). \n\nBecome a newsletter subscriber here: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/subscribe\n\nExplore Ethan's website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n\nEthan's leadership development courses https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
    "published": "2025-05-02T12:00:33.000Z"
