    "id": "fresh-alXCwqILsDk",
    "title": "5 Mistakes Stopping You from Getting Promoted",
    "deck": "A new public video from Ethan Evans.",
    "topic": "career-growth",
    "topicLabel": "Career Growth & Promotion",
    "tags": [
      "Promotion & advancement"
    ],
    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=alXCwqILsDk",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "coral",
    "description": "In this career chat with Sally Ivester (Google), we dive into the critical mistakes that may be silently stalling your career growth, and what you can do to be seen as the obvious choice for the next big opportunity.\n\n📌 Key Topics Covered: \n\n• 00:00:00 → Mistake #1: Being heads down and assuming good work speaks for itself\n• 00:01:48 → Why you must make it easy for your manager to advocate for you\n• 00:02:54 → Overcoming fear of sharing your wins without sounding like you’re bragging\n• 00:03:54 → Building executive trust: clarity, ownership, and communication\n• 00:05:00 → Mistake #2: Communicating updates vs. influencing decisions\n• 00:05:59 → Using the “What → So What → Now What” framework to speak like a leader\n• 00:06:48 → Mistake #3: Undervaluing strategic relationships and building allies\n• 00:08:23 → How to show up and stay visible to senior leadership\n• 00:09:17 → Mistake #4: Delivering fast work without clarity and executive formatting\n• 00:10:03 → Tips for writing concise, mobile-friendly emails to executives\n• 00:11:22 → Mistake #5: Expecting promotions too fast without proving repeatable impact\n• 00:13:38 → Four steps to earn leadership trust and fast-track your career\n\n💡 Key Takeaways to Accelerate Your Career: \n\n✔️ Stop relying solely on great work—make your impact obvious\n✔️ Update and manage your manager proactively\n✔️ Speak with clarity and influence, not just provide status reports\n✔️ Build strong strategic relationships across leadership layers\n✔️ Focus on undeniable strengths, not just ticking every box\n✔️ Be macro patient, but micro impatient: daily actions compound into big wins\n✔️ Simplify your communication—less is more when talking to busy execs\n\n🎯 Want to get promoted faster? Start with these actions: 📖 Recommended resource: Executive Presence by Sylvia Ann Hewlett – master how to project leadership\n\n💼 Practice the \"What, So What, Now What\" communication model\n\n🔗 Build your skip-level network and volunteer for visibility-building opportunities\n\n🔔 Subscribe for more career growth tactics!\n\n💬 Drop your questions about promotions and leadership skills in the comments!\n\n🔗 More Resources\n🔹 Connect with Ethan Evans on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n🔹 Explore Ethan Evans website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n🔹 Check out leadership & career development courses: https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
    "published": "2025-05-01T04:00:03.000Z"
