    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eF321zQijmc",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "violet",
    "description": "Annie Duke (former and very successful Professional Poker Player, Bestselling Author, & Decision-Making Expert), Alex Hart (Engineering Leader & Level Up Community Member), & Jason Yoong (COO at Level Up) discuss how to make better high stakes decisions, empower your team to make higher quality decisions without you, balance making the “best” decision vs making a “good enough” decision for the sake of speed/time, and how to know to call it quits.\n\nGet 25% off Annie's (very popular and highly rated 4.8/5) course 'Make Better Decisions' using the discount code 'LEVELUP25' at checkout here: https://maven.com/annie-duke/make-better-decisions \n\n---------\nAbout Annie Duke\nAnnie loves to dive deep into decision making under uncertainty. Her latest obsession is on the topic of quitting. In particular, she is on a mission to rehabilitate the term and get people to be proud of walking away from things.\n\n​Annie is an author, speaker, and consultant in the decision-making space, as well as Special Partner focused on Decision Science at First Round Capital Partners, a seed stage venture fund. Annie’s latest book, \"Quit: The Power of Knowing When to Walk Away\", was released in 2022 from Portfolio, a Penguin Random House imprint. Her previous book, \"Thinking in Bets\", is a national bestseller. As a former professional poker player, she has won more than $4 million in tournament poker. During her career, Annie won a World Series of Poker bracelet and is the only woman to have won the World Series of Poker Tournament of Champions and the NBC National Poker Heads-Up Championship. She retired from the game in 2012. \n\nPrior to becoming a professional poker player, Annie was awarded a National Science Foundation Fellowship to study Cognitive Psychology at the University of Pennsylvania. In 2023 Annie completed her PhD in Cognitive Psychology at UPenn.\n\n​Annie is the co-founder of The Alliance for Decision Education, a non-profit whose mission is to improve lives by empowering students through decision skills education: https://alliancefordecisioneducation.org/\n\nShe is a member of the National Board of After-School All-Stars and the Board of Directors of the Franklin Institute.\n\n​Learn more about Annie here: https://www.annieduke.com/\n\n​Subscribe to Annie's newsletter: https://annieduke.substack.com/\n\n'Thinking in Bets' book: https://a.co/d/6HK8LKs\n\n'Quit: The Power of Knowing When to Walk Away' book: https://a.co/d/bCIsVNv\n\nGet 25% off Annie's (very popular and highly rated 4.8/5) course 'Make Better Decisions' using the discount code 'LEVELUP25' at checkout here: https://maven.com/annie-duke/make-better-decisions \n\n​Course alumni testimonials:\n​-- \"This is course change completely your mindset about what it means to make good decisions.\" — CEO\n\n​-- \"Annie combines deep expertise, boundless enthusiasm and a talent for engaging students in conversation. This was the best online course I've ever taken. Highly recommended.\" — Partner\n\n​-- \"Wow! Annie is an incredible source of knowledge on decision-making. The class discussions were engaging, thought-provoking, and highly practical. The final class was absolutely phenomenal! I would highly recommend this course to anyone dedicated to improving their decision-making skills, both professionally and personally.\" — Senior Director\n\n---------\nAbout Alex Hart\nAlex is an engineering leader and Level Up Community Member. He took Annie's course and highly recommends it. \n\nConnect with Alex on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexhart23/\n\n---------\nAbout Jason Yoong\nJason has run multiple $1B+ businesses across eCommerce, marketplaces, advertising, and media. He's led 40+ person organizations, owned department P&L, managed $400M+ marketing budgets for Fortune 100 entertainment (movies and TV) and consumer electronics clients, and served as an Advisory Board Member.\n\nAfter leading and building at publicly traded companies Amazon, Dentsu Aegis, and Universal McCann (IPG), Jason joined the founding team of a venture-backed software startup and raised $8M seed.\n\nJason is now building Level Up: Your source for executive insights, high performance habits, and specific career growth actions with Ethan Evans (retired Amazon Vice President). He also serves on the Harvard Business Review advisory council and as a mentor at First Round Capital and Techstars.\n\nConnect with Jason on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/jasonyoong/\n\n---------\nAbout Level Up\nLevel Up is your source for executive insights, high performance habits, and specific career growth actions with Ethan Evans (retired Amazon VP; LinkedIn Top Voice) and Jason Yoong (COO). \n\nBecome a newsletter subscriber here: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/subscribe\n\nExplore Ethan's website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n\nEthan's leadership development courses https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
