    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sTeDD0KPyqA",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "orange",
    "description": "In this excerpt from a chat with Coach Alisa Cohn, we explore the deep fears that hold people back from joining startups—and how to move past them. If you’ve ever wondered whether you should stay at your safe job or leap into the chaos and creativity of startup life, this conversation is packed with wisdom from a seasoned leadership coach.\n\n📌 Key Topics Covered:\n• 00:00:05 → Why people hesitate to join startups\n• 00:00:27 → Frameworks for identifying and facing your fears\n• 00:01:12 → Common fears: failure, success, and the unknown\n• 00:01:56 → Comparing “career baskets”: startup vs. corporate\n• 00:02:34 → The reality of less support in startups\n• 00:03:18 → Knowing your values and how they align with startup life\n• 00:04:08 → Handling the financial fear of leaving a job\n• 00:05:23 → Ego and identity risks: “What if I fail?”\n• 00:06:13 → Planning worst-case scenarios to reduce fear\n• 00:07:16 → How fear of the unknown stops progress\n• 00:08:13 → What makes the startup “basket” amazing\n• 00:08:57 → Making real impact and rapid progress in startups\n• 00:09:24 → Fast-tracked leadership growth in startup roles\n• 00:09:54 → Mission-driven teams and how they elevate your career\n\n💡 Key Takeaways for Navigating Career Risk:\n✔️ Name your fears clearly—don’t let them stay vague and powerful\n✔️ Compare your current job’s benefits and constraints with what a startup offers\n✔️ Assess your true financial flexibility and risk tolerance\n✔️ Make a “worst-case scenario” plan—most fears are less scary when written out\n✔️ Startups are chaotic, but they offer fast growth, deep impact, and passionate teams\n\n🔗 More Resources\n🔹 Connect with Ethan Evans on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n🔹 Explore Ethan Evans website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n🔹 Check out leadership & career development courses: https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
