    "title": "Interview FAQs- How to Answer the Hardest Interview Questions",
    "deck": "A new public video from Ethan Evans.",
    "topic": "career-growth",
    "topicLabel": "Career Growth & Promotion",
    "tags": [],
    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=34cywIhbfEI",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "coral",
    "description": "In this excerpt from a live stream, Ethan Evans breaks down how to answer tough interview questions, from handling conflict with a coworker to discussing your biggest weakness and addressing gaps in your resume. This talk is packed with actionable insights to help you navigate job interviews confidently.\n\nTimestamps & Key Takeaways:\n\n• 00:00:00 – Introduction: How to handle difficult interview questions\n• 00:00:19 – How to talk about workplace conflict using the STAR method\n• 00:02:13 – Why interviewers ask conflict-related questions & what they are looking for\n• 00:03:03 – The “Biggest Weakness” trap question—what NOT to say\n• 00:04:19 – Real weaknesses vs. fake weaknesses (and how to frame them properly)\n• 00:05:09 – Tips on demonstrating self-awareness and personal growth\n• 00:05:47 – Which interview questions you should decline to answer (illegal or inappropriate questions)\n• 00:08:06 – How companies use sneaky tactics to gather personal information\n• 00:09:58 – How to discuss past jobs that ended on a bad note (without badmouthing anyone)\n• 00:12:30 – Handling the question: “Why were you laid off?”\n• 00:14:32 – How to talk about a failure in an interview (What was the failure? What did you learn? What would you do differently?)\n• 00:17:24 – What to do if you don’t know the answer to a coding question in an interview\n• 00:18:54 – The hiring decision process: How many no votes mean rejection?\n• 00:21:17 – The impact of attitude in interviews—why anger and frustration work against you\n• 00:23:17 – How to explain gaps in your resume (and turn them into positives)\n• 00:26:10 – What interviewers really want to know about you\n• 00:26:52 – The right way to answer “Tell me about yourself” (without oversharing)\n• 00:30:14 – How much time should you spend preparing stock answers for interview questions?\n\n Key Takeaways:\n\n✔ Use the STAR method (Situation, Task, Action, Result) for structured responses\n✔ Avoid fake weaknesses (e.g., “I work too hard”)—be honest but show self-improvement\n✔ Never answer illegal questions (e.g., age, marital status, race, or personal background)\n✔ Frame past job exits in a positive light—focus on what you’re moving toward, not what you’re leaving\n✔ When discussing failures, highlight what you learned and how you improved\n✔ If stuck on a technical question, ask for hints rather than wasting time\n✔ Be mindful that attitude and confidence can make or break your chances\n\n📌 About Ethan Evans\nEthan Evans is a leadership and career coach with extensive experience in hiring, interviewing, and professional development. His insights help job seekers and professionals level up their careers.\n\n🔗 More Resources\n🔹 Connect with Ethan Evans on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n🔹 Explore Ethan Evans website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n🔹 Check out leadership & career development courses: https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
