    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q6IlEgAw2kY",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "orange",
    "description": "In this career coaching session, we break down the strategies and resume adjustments needed to successfully transition from a full-time technical role (like DevOps) to a Technical Program Manager (TPM) position.\n\n📌 Key Topics Covered:\n\n00:00:05 → How to shift from a technical role to TPM\n00:01:20 → Internal vs. external job transitions & risk factors\n00:02:29 → Resume mistakes: Why your cover letter isn't enough\n00:03:16 → Structuring your resume for TPM roles (highlighting relevant experience)\n00:04:49 → The importance of action words: Avoiding \"worked on\" and \"part of\"\n00:06:05 → Using leadership-focused language to showcase initiative\n00:08:11 → How to show business impact and accountability in your resume\n00:09:23 → Why TPM roles require strong data-driven skills & structured work methods\n\n💡 Key Takeaways to Optimize Your Resume for a TPM Role:\n\n✔️ Add an objective that clearly states you are transitioning into a TPM role\n✔️ Highlight program management experience, even if it was informal in past jobs\n✔️ Use strong action verbs like “Created, Led, Drove” instead of “Worked on”\n✔️ Showcase business impact and measurable results from past projects\n✔️ Demonstrate your ability to influence teams, work against deadlines, and manage initiatives\n\n🎯 Want to successfully land a TPM role? Start here:\n\n📖 Recommended reading: What Color is Your Parachute? – A practical guide for career transitions\n💼 Certifications to consider: PMP, Scrum Master, and Agile training\n🔗 Network for referrals on LinkedIn – A crucial step for breaking into TPM positions\n\n📌 About this Series:\n\nThis discussion is part of a career transition coaching series, helping professionals move from technical execution roles into leadership positions in program management.\n🔔 Subscribe for more career insights!\n💬 Drop your career transition questions in the comments!\n\n🔗 More Resources\n🔹 Connect with Ethan Evans on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n🔹 Explore Ethan Evans website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n🔹 Check out leadership & career development courses: https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
