    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "lime",
    "description": "In this deep-dive career coaching session, our guest Shivang seeks expert advice on transitioning from DevOps to a Technical Program Manager (TPM) role. \n\nThis conversation covers: \n\n📌 How to refine your resume to stand out for TPM roles\n📌 The key skills and certifications that hiring managers value\n📌 The role of PMP, Scrum Master, and BI tools in a TPM career\n📌 How to land recruiter calls at top tech companies (FAANG and beyond)\n📌 Strategies for making a successful career transition without an MBA\n\n🔹 Key Takeaways from the Discussion:\n\n00:00:05 → Resume mistakes: Why \"working on\" doesn't show leadership\n00:02:26 → Using action words and business impact in your resume\n00:03:44 → The real value of PMP certification & keyword optimization\n00:05:18 → Why recruiters keep categorizing Siobhan as DevOps\n00:06:49 → PMP vs. PBA: Which one is better for TPM roles?\n00:08:07 → Is BI (AWS Quicksight, Tableau, Power BI) a must-have for TPMs?\n00:09:32 → The most crucial soft skill: Holding people accountable without alienating them\n00:10:59 → The best way to land a recruiter call at FAANG companies\n00:14:45 → Interview psychology: Why first impressions decide your job offer\n00:19:57 → TPM vs. Technical Product Manager (TPdM): Career growth paths\n00:24:27 → How to position past project management experience to land TPM roles\n\n💡 Want to break into a TPM role? Here’s your strategy:\n\n1️. Optimize your resume with strong action words and measurable impact\n2️. Get a PMP or Scrum Master certification for credibility\n3️. Network for referrals—cold applications rarely work at FAANG\n4️. Show leadership and cross-functional collaboration in past projects\n5️. Learn financial modeling and business analysis if you want to pivot into Product Management\n\n🎯 Resources Mentioned:\n📖 What Color is Your Parachute? – A must-read for career transitions\n🎓 PMP & Scrum Master Certifications – Worth it or not?\n📊 Business Intelligence Tools – AWS Quicksight, Tableau, Power BI\n🔗 Connect with recruiters on LinkedIn for referrals\n\n📌 About this Series:\n\nThis career coaching session is designed for engineers, developers, and tech professionals looking to transition into leadership and program management roles.\n🔔 Subscribe for more career strategy insights!\n💬 Drop your questions in the comments—what’s your biggest career challenge?\n\n🔗 More Resources\n🔹 Connect with Ethan Evans on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n🔹 Explore Ethan Evans website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n🔹 Check out leadership & career development courses: https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
