    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "green",
    "description": "In this excerpt from his conversation with @cloudwithraj,  Ethan Evans (Former VP at Amazon) shares career-defining strategies for individual contributors in tech. Learn how to develop soft skills, improve influence without authority, build a powerful network, avoid layoffs, and plan your long-term career progression.\n\n🔹 Timestamps & Key Sections\n\n00:00:00 Introduction – Why soft skills matter as much as technical expertise.\n\n00:00:17 The Most Valuable Skills Beyond Technical Chops\n\n- The importance of soft skills (communication, collaboration, emotional intelligence).\n\n- Why investing in these skills leads to faster career growth.\nThe 80/20 rule: Why small improvements in soft skills yield massive returns.\n\n00:02:12 -The Power of Influence in Tech\n\n- Why technical brilliance alone isn’t enough.\n\n- How to win support for your ideas without direct authority.\n\n- Understanding resistance: Why smart people argue against good ideas.\n\n00:04:05 How to Build a Powerful Network (Beyond Just LinkedIn Connections)\n\n- Why providing value is the key to building relationships.\n\n- The secret to growing an engaged network inside and outside work.\n\n- How niche interests (even something like Wookie culture) can create unexpected career connections.\n\n00:07:02 Why Your Network Today Becomes Your Career Leverage Tomorrow\n\n00:09:16 How to Avoid Getting Laid Off in Tech\n\n- Understanding how layoff decisions are really made.\n\n- Why \"quiet quitting\" makes you an easy target.\n\n- How to stay off the cut list by making yourself indispensable.\n\n- The mistake Ethan made that got him laid off twice—and what he learned.\n\n00:12:03 Should You Proactively Look for Other Roles?\n\n00:13:32 How to Plan Your Career (5-10 Years Ahead)\n\n- Why most tech professionals struggle to see their long-term path.\n\n- The power of compound growth—both in finances and career.\n\n-How to shift from scarcity mindset to abundance thinking.\n\n00:16:58 When to Quit & What to Consider Before Leaving a High-Paying Job\n\n- How Ethan decided to leave Amazon after reaching VP level.\n\n- The mental traps that keep people working longer than necessary.\n\n- How to set a “freedom number” and actually stick to it.\n\n00:19:42 The Problem with Always Wanting More\n\n00:21:42 How to Manage Time, Energy & Focus Like a High Performer\n\n🎯 Who Should Watch This?\n\n✅ Tech professionals looking to grow beyond technical skills.\n✅ Engineers & individual contributors aiming for leadership influence.\n✅ Anyone who wants to build a stronger network & career safety net.\n\n🔗 Connect with Ethan Evans & Explore More\n📍 Follow Ethan on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n📧 Subscribe to Ethan’s Leadership Newsletter: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/\n📚 Take Ethan’s Leadership Courses: https://maven.com/courses?query=ethan+evans",
