    "accent": "orange",
    "description": "Jeff Bezos was furious. My career was over.\n\nHear how Ethan Evans, former Amazon VP, survived a catastrophic product launch, earned back Bezos’ trust, and got promoted despite public failure.\nLearn the exact steps he took to turn disaster into redemption.\n\nTIMESTAMPS & KEY MOMENTS\n\n00:00 - Intro: “This failure almost ended my career…”\n01:02 - The Launch Disaster: Test Drive feature crashes at 6 AM (Jeff’s email fury)\n03:08 - “Jeff copied my boss’s boss. It was a bloodbath.”\n04:24 - Recovery Hack: “Buy time with 1-hour updates” (script included)\n05:18 - AWS engineers’ brutal fix: “We’ll brute-force 500 servers”\n06:30 - Bezos’ Saturday night ambush: “I broke it again”\n07:11 - Face-to-Face with Bezos: “I sat next to his chair. Here’s what he said…”\n08:48 - Redemption: Promoted to VP 2 years later\n09:32 - Key takeaway: “If I survived Bezos, you can survive ANY failure”\n\nKEY LESSONS\n\n04:24: “Own it. Say ‘It’s my fault’ before they blame you.”\n05:18: “When failing, beg for help—even rivals will rescue you.”\n07:11: “I sat inches from Bezos. His 7-word question changed everything.”\n09:32: “CEOs forget failures if you deliver comebacks.”\n\nAVOID THESE MISTAKES\n\nHiding from angry leaders (Ethan’s “chicken meeting” tactic).\nOver-engineering fixes during crises (500 servers  or perfect code).\n\nView the full video over on Lenny's channel @LennysPodcast \n\n🔔 Subscribe for more crisis leadership tips\n📥 Read the newsletter: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/\n💬 Tell us your disaster experiences in the comments\n\n#JeffBezos #Amazon #Leadership #CareerGrowth #Failure #Workplace #Management #Startup #Tech #Success",
