    "tags": [],
    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O0-XoEv8jvk",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "green",
    "description": "In this conversation, Yuzheng Sun (Staff Data Scientist at Statsig; Prev. Meta, Amazon, Tencent) interviews Ethan Evans (retired Amazon VP) on the essence of effective leadership and management within tech companies. \n\nKey takeaways:\n1/ Ethan underscored that a manager's true power lies not in their individual contributions but in how they harness the collective strengths of their team. He stressed the importance of nurturing all team members—from top performers to those who may be struggling—highlighting that overlooking any segment could be a costly mistake.\n\n2/ Ethan illustrated the multifaceted role of managers as negotiators and influencers. They had to adeptly manage peer relationships, dependencies, and resources to create an environment for innovation. As leaders ascended to director-level positions, their focus shifted to making strategic impacts on the company — driving revenue, reducing costs, and enhancing customer satisfaction.\n\n3/ A particularly compelling part of the discussion revolved around influencing others without authority. Ethan shared his experience at Twitch, where, without formal power, he effectively guided leadership by asking, \"Could I share how I've seen this done elsewhere?\" This approach opened doors to collaboration, allowing leaders to present valuable insights without triggering defensiveness.\n\n4/ Ultimately, Ethan emphasized the importance of building trust and demonstrating genuine intent to help. By positioning oneself as a collaborative partner rather than an adversary, leaders could influence decisions and drive positive change, even in challenging situations.\n\nYuzheng's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/yuzhengsun/\nEthan's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n\nSubscribe to Ethan's career growth newsletter & community: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/\n\nAbout Ethan:\nIn Ethan's 15+ years at Amazon, he led global teams of 800+ and invented well-known businesses and products such as Prime Video, Amazon Video, Amazon Appstore, Merch by Amazon, Prime Gaming (formerly Twitch Prime), and Twitch Commerce. Ethan holds 70+ patents. Has reviewed 10,000+ resumes, conducted 2,500+ interviews, and 1,000+ hires. Was an Amazon Bar Raiser and Bar Raiser Core Leader, responsible for training and maintaining Amazon's group of interview outcome facilitators. And helped advocate for and draft the Amazon Leadership Principle (LP) “Ownership” — the words, “They never say ‘that’s not my job.’” are Ethan's.",
