    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V_fgMqcAbUI",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "rose",
    "description": "Jamie A. Lee (Walmart, Nike, EA, Sony, Vital Proteins, and Everlane) and Jason Yoong discuss executive 1-pagers and getting executive buy-in.\n\nJamie shares her experience leading digital initiatives for major brands like Nike, Walmart, EA, and emerging brands like Vital Proteins. Highlights include how to structure an executive summary, the importance of aligning goals and metrics, addressing risks, and strategies to build executive trust and credibility. Jamie also offers insights on navigating executive meetings, maintaining relationships with executives, and balancing priorities within different organizational contexts.\n\n---------\nTopics discussed:\n00:00 Introduction\n01:38 Overview of the One Page Executive Summary\n02:28 Key Components: Vision and Objectives\n04:01 From-To Analysis and Goals\n05:06 Strategies, Metrics, and Enablers\n08:25 Common Executive Questions and Challenges\n10:56 Presenting and Prioritizing Goals\n18:15 Building Executive Buy-In and Credibility\n22:53 Aligning Team Goals with Business Objectives\n23:23 Creating a Shared Language for Strategy\n24:04 Showcasing Initiative and Testing Strategies\n24:45 Pre-Meeting Preparation and Aligning Allies\n25:24 Speaking Up in Executive Meetings\n30:10 Maintaining Executive Relationships Post-Launch\n36:04 Career Growth: Big Business vs. Startup Teams\n37:38 Lessons from Big Companies and Emerging Brands\n41:02 Vital Proteins to Nestle Acquisition: Key Insights\n44:26 Final Thoughts and Jamie's Course Information\n\n---------\nAbout Jamie A. Lee\n​​​Jamie is a seasoned eCommerce executive with over 14 years of expertise driving digital and omnichannel growth for brands like Nike, Walmart, EA, Sony, and emerging brands like Vital Proteins and Everlane.\n\n​Jamie was part of the founding team that scaled Walmart's Online Grocery service from market 1 to over 1000, building Nike's new Global Apparel eCommerce organization as Digital GM and launching new product lines (Hijab, Yoga, Maternity), and as VP of Digital, leading Vital Protein's eCommerce team to profitable growth and completing a full Nestle acquisition.\n\n​Jamie is an instructor on Maven, teaching eCommerce 201, and has spoken at conferences such as eTail (West & East flagship events) on topics like digital growth, acquisition, and profitability. She has also served as a keynote speaker at events held by her alma mater, UC Berkeley (MBA) and the University of Southern California (Bachelors), as well as UC Dublin.\n\n​Her contributions to the eCommerce field have been recognized, with recent honors including being named one of the 30 Most Influential in eCommerce in '22 and Top Women in Retail on the Rise in '21.\n\n​Follow Jamie on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/jamieannlee/\n\nJamie's Maven course eCommerce 201: https://maven.com/jamie-a-lee/ecom\n\nBook Jamie for 1:1 coaching: https://www.jamiealee.com/\n\n---------\nAbout Level Up\n​​​Level Up is your source for career growth solutions & community.\n\nJoin here: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/subscribe\n\nJason Yoong is the operating partner at Level Up (and ex-Amazon).\n\nConnect with Jason on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/jasonyoong/\n\nExplore Ethan's website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n\nEthan's leadership development courses https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
    "published": "2024-10-16T19:00:15.000Z"
