    "format": "Conversation",
    "sourceLabel": "Auto-discovered",
    "sourceNote": "Auto-discovered from Ethan’s public YouTube channel with YouTube Data API; review before publishing.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-BAdkBGjOIlccGLZ3jbLiA",
    "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uO0dI_tCvUU",
    "duration": "Watch on YouTube",
    "accent": "violet",
    "description": "​​​​​​​​​Level Up Newsletter & Community paid members were invited to join this live event with Andrew Yeung and Jason Yoong discussing \"How to Be a High-Value Connector & Networker\".\n\n---------\nTopics discussed:\n00:00 Introduction and Welcome\n00:46 Common Networking Mistakes\n01:54 Building Goodwill in Networking\n04:03 Effective Cold Outreach Strategies\n09:05 Creating and Controlling the Room\n24:59 Balancing Corporate and Entrepreneurial Pursuits\n29:07 Maximizing Your Efforts\n29:30 Navigating Networking\n32:20 Internal and External Networking Strategies\n34:39 The Importance of Building Relationships\n35:04 Soft Skills at Big Tech Companies\n36:25 Performance Reviews and Networking\n40:02 Building a Personal Brand\n42:30 Organizing Successful Events\n44:13 Reflecting on Big Company Experiences\n50:12 Future Plans and Community Support\n\n---------\nAbout Andrew Yeung\nAndrew is an ex-Google and Meta product leader turned tech and hospitality entrepreneur and investor.\n\nHe hosts events and runs Andrew's Mixers (1,000+ person tech rooftop mixers), The Junto Series (C-suite and tech leader dinners), and Lumos House (a multi-day, multi-city experience in a private mansion). Over 30,000 people have attended across 8 cities. Attendees include founders of billion-dollar companies, media personalities with millions of followers, and Olympic athletes turned entrepreneurs.\n\nBusiness Insider dubbed Andrew the \"Gatsby of Silicon Alley.\"\n\n​Andrew recently launched The OOO Summit.\n​1) The Os stand for Owners, Operators, and Outliers.\n\n​2) It's a full-day event, with talks, activities, networking sessions, and of course a “party”, for you to learn from the top experts in the biz and meet some of the most ambitious, curious, and inspiring people in New York City.\n​\n3) If you have even the slightest itch to build something, then you might want to consider attending.\n\nPartners and sponsors of his events include Fidelity, Craft Ventures, Techstars, Rho, Silicon Valley Bank, and many more. Andrew has also been featured on the front page of Business Insider, Fast Company, Bloomberg, Fortune Magazine, Morning Brew, and This Week in Startups for building tech communities.\n\nBeyond that, Andrew invests in early-stage companies as a Partner at Next Wave NYC, a pre-seed venture fund backed by Flybridge. Writes on Business Insider, his personal blog (www.andrew.today), and has spoken about tech careers, community, and entrepreneurship at Princeton University, Columbia Business School, SXSW, Advertising Week, and Jason Calacanis' podcast.\n\nAndrews online platform also spans 120,000+ tech leaders, founders, and operators, and reaches 1M+ people every month. With this platform, he's helped hundreds of founders raise money, hire talent, and scale their companies.\n\nPitch Andrew at andrew@andrewsmixers.com\nBook time with Andrew: https://intro.co/andrewyeung\n​Follow Andrew on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/andyeung/\n​Follow Andrew on Twitter: https://twitter.com/andruyeung\nThe OOO Summit: https://carry.com/ooo\nAndrew's Mixers: https://www.andrewsmixers.com/\nThe Junto Series: https://www.linkedin.com/company/juntoclubseries/\nLumos House: https://thelumoshouse.com/\n\n---------\nAbout Level Up\n​​​Level Up is your source for career growth solutions & community by retired Amazon Vice President, Ethan Evans.\n\nPaid members get access to member-only events, all newsletter articles, access to a private Slack leadership networking community, and more. \n\nJoin here: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/p/level-up-career-community\n\n​​​​​​Jason Yoong is the operating partner at Level Up (and ex-Amazon).\n\nConnect with Jason on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/jasonyoong/\n\nExplore Ethan's website: https://www.ethanevans.com/\n\nEthan's leadership development courses https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)",
    "published": "2024-07-11T20:12:38.000Z"
