    "accent": "amber",
    "description": "In this 6-minute clip, Ameesh Paleja (EVP at Capital One, ex-Google VP, ex-OfferUp CTO, Atom Tickets CoFounder & CEO, ex-Amazon Director) shares what he learned from Ethan as his direct report at Amazon. \n\nWatch the full 1 hour and 47-minute chat between Ethan and Ameesh where they discuss Ameesh's career from Engineer to CEO & EVP: https://youtu.be/0713FMGVnQc?feature=shared\n\n---------\n​Backstory: Ethan and Ameesh\n​I (Ethan) joined Amazon in 2005. Ameesh joined my new team as the most senior engineer. The team was 6 people. Ameesh was the only SDE II, with 4 total years of experience. One team member had 2 years, one had 1 year, and 3 were new college grads. Thus, Ameesh had more experience than the other 5 members combined.\n\n​Ameesh is a natural leader and took the role of lead engineer on the first version of Prime Video.\n\n​While working with me, Ameesh was promoted first to SDE III, then switched to Manager. He was promoted to Senior Manager (Amazon L7) while working on Prime Video.\n\n​Ameesh and I switched to video games and then to build the Amazon Appstore. Ameesh moved to Orange County to be closer to his family. He built a new office for the Amazon Appstore, ultimately with 300 people, and was promoted to Director (Amazon L8).\n\n​Ameesh left Amazon to found his own startup, Atom Tickets.\n\n---------\nAbout Ameesh Paleja\n​​Ameesh is an EVP at Capital One, a Board Member at Everchron, and an Advisor to The Professional Collegiate League.\n\n​​Prior, Ameesh served as VP of Engineering at Google, CTO at OfferUp, CoFounder & CEO at Atom Tickets, and Director at Amazon (where he started as a Sr. Software Engineer).\n\n​Follow Ameesh on LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ameesh/\n\n---------\nLive attendance at this event was exclusive to Level Up Career Community members.\n\nLevel Up is your source for career growth solutions & community:\n(A) Free members get 4 full newsletter articles a month.\n\n(B) Paid members get 8 articles + exclusive access to ongoing live podcasts/events (e.g. career talks, watching live executive coaching with a real client, fireside chats w/leaders, career Q&A) + all video recordings (16+ hours to date) + a private Slack community for leadership networking.\n\nRead about membership benefits, testimonials, video highlights, and join here: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/p/level-up-career-community\n\n---------\nAbout Ethan Evans:\nIn Ethan's 15+ years at Amazon, he led global teams of 800+ and invented well-known businesses and products such as Prime Video, Amazon Video, Amazon Appstore, Merch by Amazon, Prime Gaming (formerly Twitch Prime), and Twitch Commerce. \n\n-- 70+ patents. \n-- Reviewed 10,000+ resumes, conducted 2,500+ interviews, and 1,000+ hires. \n-- Was an Amazon Bar Raiser and Bar Raiser Core Leader, responsible for training and maintaining Amazon's group of interview outcome facilitators. \n-- Helped advocate for and draft the Amazon Leadership Principle (LP) “Ownership” — the words, “They never say ‘that’s not my job.’” are Ethan's. \n\nEthan's LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethanevansvp/\n\nEthan's leadership development courses https://maven.com/ethan-evans (live online) and https://ethan-evans.mykajabi.com/ (on-demand)\n\nBecome a Level Up member: https://levelupwithethanevans.substack.com/p/level-up-career-community",
